CC   MIR167a is found on chromosome 3 in Arabidopsis thaliana [1] and is
CC   thought, like miR160, to target mRNAs coding for auxin response factors,
CC   DNA binding proteins that are thought to control transcription in response
CC   to the phytohormone auxin. Transcriptional regulation is important for
CC   many of the diverse developmental responses to auxin signals, which
CC   include cell elongation, division, and differentiation in both roots and
CC   shoots [2].
