CC   MIR168a is found on chromosome 4 in Arabidopsis thaliana [1] and is
CC   thought to target mRNAs coding for Argonaute (AGO1), which is required for
CC   axillary shoot meristem formation and leaf development in Arabidopsis. It
CC   has been suggested that AGO1 may also influence miRNA accumulation in
CC   plants and that miR168 may act as a negative-feedback mechanism for
CC   controlling expression of the AGO1 gene [2].
