CC   Mouse miR-9 was cloned from mouse brain tissues in [1].  There are 3
CC   predicted hairpin precursor structures in the mouse genome, each has a
CC   closely related human homologue [3].  Two copies of mir-9-1
CC   (MIR:MI0000720) are found as part of a larger duplicated region on mouse
CC   chromosome 3, mir-9-2 (MIR:MI0000157, previously named mir-9 here) is
CC   found on chromosome 13, and mir-9-3 (MIR:MI0000721) on chromosome 7.
CC   miR-9* was described as miR-131 in reference [1], but appears to be
CC   expressed from the opposite arm of all 3 mir-9 predicted stem-loops.
