CC   miR-7 was predicted by computational methods using conservation between
CC   mouse, human and Fugu rubripes sequences [1].  Expression of the excised
CC   miR has been validated in zebrafish, and the 5' end mapped by PCR.  The 3'
CC   end was not experimentally determined.  This sequence represents the mouse
CC   homologue of human mir-7-3 -- the derived mature form differs at a single
CC   position from that expressed from mir-7-1 (MIR:MI0000728) and mir-7-2
CC   (MIR:MI0000729) in mouse, and mir-7-1 (MIR:MI0000263), mir-7-2
CC   (MIR:MI0000264) and mir-7-3 (MIR:MI0000265) in human.
