RT   elegans";
RL   Nature. 426:845-849(2003).
XX
RN   [2]
RX   PUBMED; 15317971.
RA   Ohler U, Yekta S, Lim LP, Bartel DP, Burge CB;
RT   "Patterns of flanking sequence conservation and a characteristic upstream
RT   motif for microRNA gene identification";
RL   RNA. 10:1309-1322(2004).
XX
CC   The bilateral taste receptor neurons ASE left (ASEL) and ASE right (ASER)
CC   are thought to be responsible for an assymetrical pattern of chemoreceptor
CC   gene expression in C. elegans.  miRNA lsy-6 is expressed in ASEL but not
CC   ASER and has been shown to control this bilateral assymetry by binding to
CC   a complementary site in the 3' UTR of cog-1, an Nkx-type homeobox gene.
CC   Johnston and Hobert determined the locus of lsy-6, and predicted the
CC   position of the mature miR sequence [1].  The miR location was refined by
CC   Ohler et al. who mapped the 5' end by PCR and confirmed the 3' end from
CC   the cloning of the miR* sequence from the opposite arm of the precursor
CC   [2].
