CC   The bilateral taste receptor neurons ASE left (ASEL) and ASE right (ASER)
CC   are thought to be responsible for an assymetrical pattern of chemoreceptor
CC   gene expression in C. elegans.  miRNA lsy-6 is expressed in ASEL but not
CC   ASER and has been shown to control this bilateral assymetry by binding to
CC   a complementary site in the 3' UTR of cog-1, an Nkx-type homeobox gene
CC   [1].  This sequence is the predicted C. briggsae homologue of miR-lsy-6
CC   from elegans.  Its expression has not been verified in briggsae.
